     4	
     5	## 1. Question
     6	
     7	What are the seen-split errors (EDT, C50, T60; K = 1 and K = 8) of the three same-budget xRIR variants — SimpleViT (xRIR), CylindricalViT and YawAug-xRIR — when each is trained under the authors' **seen protocol**, so that the paper-style table has both split columns for all three rows? No hypothesis is pre-registered beyond the table; the paired differences between arms on the seen split are reported descriptively with intervals.
     8	
     9	## 2. Protocol and arms
    10	
    11	- **Seen protocol** (authors' `treble_xRIR_seen_dataset.py`, pinned by exp_03 — never edited): test = the 6 217 source–receiver pairs of `seen_test_split.pkl` (131 rooms); train = every other RIR of the dataset = 296 454 files (9 265 micro-batches of 32 per epoch, the last one holding 6 examples instead of the unseen protocol's 14; with the trainer's accumulation rule 4 633 updates per epoch, 12 epochs = 55 596 updates versus the unseen protocol's 55 572, +24 updates = +0.043 %). All 131 test rooms have other receivers in the training set (630 receivers are held out); of the 6 217 test pairs, 5 124 lie in the unseen protocol's training set and 1 093 in its 17 test rooms — under the seen protocol every test room is a trained room. Train/test target overlap is 0.
    12	- **Arms** (three new 12-epoch trainings, one realisation each; the M tier, dim 512 / depth 12 / heads 8 / mlp 512): `seen_simple` (xRIR control, `--backbone simple`), `seen_cyl` (`--backbone cylindrical`), `seen_aug` (`--backbone simple --yaw-aug 1 --yaw-aug-seed 0 --yaw-aug-width 512`). Recipe otherwise identical to exp_01/exp_04/exp_05: `--num-shot 8 --max-len 9600 --lr 1e-3 --weight-decay 1e-4 --decay-epochs 3 --lr-gamma 0.1 --epochs 12 --batch-size 32 --accum-steps 2 --num-workers 12 --seed 0 --tf32 --log-interval 50 --save-every 0 --epoch-ckpt-every 1`, plus the new `--protocol seen`. `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`, `OMP_NUM_THREADS=2`, interpreter `/home/yixunhu/miniconda3/envs/xRIR/bin/python`. Contract per arm vs its unseen-protocol twin: **same recipe and epoch budget, the protocol (training set) being the intended change**; training trajectories are not paired (single realisation each; unordered-set path listing and worker-local reference draws as before). The trainer's `--protocol unseen` default reproduces the current behaviour bit for bit (parity test as exp_05 §7 item 6). For `seen_aug` the yaw counter is `t = (epoch − 1)·B + batch_idx` with `B = 9 265` (loader length, exp_04 A4), domain 0…111 179, same mixer/seed/overflow guard; offsets at equal (epoch, batch_idx) therefore differ from exp_04's from epoch 2 on — a consequence of the protocol-dependent loader length, recorded, not a defect. Normalised-args comparison against exp_01's control: historical absent fields → explicitly checked defaults (as exp_05 §7 item 6); operational exclusions `save_dir, save_every, epoch_ckpt_every, PYTHONHASHSEED, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`; permitted intended differences `protocol` (all three arms) and `yaw_aug, yaw_aug_seed, yaw_aug_width` (`seen_aug` only); derived fields (`train_batches_per_epoch` = 9 265, `param_counts`, `tier` = M, `env`) validated separately, never diffed.
    13	- **Evaluation**: the seen split, all 6 217 queries, K = 8 and K = 1, at k = 0 only, condition P, batch 16, TF32 off; **five evaluation seeds {42, 43, 44, 45, 46}** with seen-split reference manifests `ckpt/exp07/reference_manifest_seen_k{8,1}_seed{s}.json` built by `tools.reference_manifest.build_manifest(seen_dataset, seed=s, num_shot=K)` (the seen dataset exposes the same `get_ir_and_location_for_other_sources` interface) and `--gl-seed s`; the evaluator is a NEW entry point `tools/exp07_eval.py` that imports `tools.exp04_eval`'s machinery and the frozen `eval_yaw_rotation` functions unchanged but constructs the **seen** test dataset (`treble_xRIR_seen_dataset.xRIR_Dataset(split='test')`) for `ManifestDataset`'s exact query-list check (the frozen `build_manifest_dataset` hard-codes the unseen dataset and would reject 6 217 ≠ 6 337 queries) and records `split = seen` plus the sha256 of `seen_test_split.pkl` in the eval manifest and metas; the eval launcher (`--entry exp07 --split seen`) binds the same, refuses a seen manifest with the unseen entry point and vice versa (cross-split rejection), keeps canonical padding, and the numerical path is proven identical to `tools/exp04_eval.py` under identical inputs (unseen 32-query parity) and to a direct `eval_yaw_rotation`-function call on a seen subset. Run-level provenance as exp_04 (immutable manifest, completion, `--bind-input train_manifest/train_completion/train_args`). 3 arms × 2 K × 5 seeds = 30 runs plus the released `xRIR_seen.pth` (sha256 `1762c702…`, pinned now) under the same five-seed protocol as a **reference row** (K = 8 and K = 1, 10 runs): 40 runs ≈ 5.3 h. Reference-row policy: external checkpoint, training budget/epoch/realisation/selection unknown, no training bindings, provenance = the file digest and the authors' release; it is a checkpoint-performance reference, not an arm of the recipe comparison. Calibration: its K = 8 five-seed result is compared with the historical full-split reproduction (0.0389 s / 1.029 dB / 7.27 %, exp_01 results.md; random references, unseeded phases, batch 1) and the difference attributed to references/phases/batch, not to the evaluator (the unseen-split parity above certifies the numerics).
    14	- **Estimand (frozen)**: metrics EDT (s in the LaTeX table, ms in the canonical JSON; SD converted with the mean), C50 (dB), T60 (%), plus loss and log-STFT MSE in the JSON; per arm × K the table cell = mean ± sample SD (ddof 1) over the five seeds of each seed's mean over its finite queries (TABLE_V1 rule; a seed whose finite count differs from the others by > 2 refuses the cell); epoch-12 checkpoints only (no test-selected epoch). Descriptive pairs (`cyl − simple`, `aug − simple`, and `released − simple` labelled reference) at K = 8 and K = 1: per query the five-seed plain mean per arm on the paired cohort (finite for all five seeds in both arms; empty cohort refuses the cell; exclusions reported per arm/seed), statistic = absolute difference of means in native units AND the relative difference (Δ/mean_simple, %) — both recomputed inside each of 20 000 query-level bootstrap resamples (seed 0; two-sided 2.5/97.5 percentile, pointwise), with an equal-weight 131-room cluster bootstrap as the secondary interval; a two-seed (0/1) convergence check is reported. **No verdict, no significance marker, no superiority/equivalence claim**; the intervals are conditional on these trained checkpoints (five evaluation seeds do not estimate training-seed variability).
