worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_05_param_efficiency_claude/plan_param_efficiency.md:29:Timing basis: the M control's measured runtime was 28.2 h for 111 132 micro-batches, i.e. ≈ 0.91 s per micro-batch including test epochs and saves (the 1.4 s/iteration figure in CLAUDE.md is an early estimate; 1.4 × 9 261 × 12 would be 43 h). The ViT runs 2 + K = 10 times per sample, so encoder FLOPs dominate: expect S ≈ 12–16 h and L ≈ 40–55 h; the §7 probes replace these guesses before launch, with a ≤ 60 h gate per arm. Cumulative ceiling: 1.5 × the probe projection per arm over all attempts; exceeding it requires renewed authorisation. Four runs ≈ 110–140 GPU-hours; on two A6000s about 3 days, scheduled around exp_04's training (GPU 0, ≈ 30 h from its launch) — coordinate GPU ownership with the exp_04 session before launching.
