## 11. v2 changelog (responses to the round-1 plan review)

1 tiered evaluation entry point `tools/exp05_eval.py` (imports the pinned evaluator, builds the registered tier from `args.json`, strict load, tier recorded, M byte-identity test, legacy-M handling); 2 micro-batch 32 × 2 mandatory for every confirmatory arm, L redesigned rather than a 16 × 4 fallback (BatchNorm and accumulation-scaling confound stated); 3 H2 registered as one four-cell family with the superiority interval [Q_0.00625, Q_0.99375] and TOST at α = 0.0125 per side ([Q_0.0125, Q_0.9875] within ±3 %), both targets fixed, relative statistic inside each resample, bootstrap seeds 0/1, convergence gate on every decision interval; 4 exp_04-equivalent provenance made mandatory, dedicated exp_05 profiles with approved closure digests, producer admission checks enumerated, parameter counting moved to the experiment-owned `tools/exp05_params.py` (no edit of exp_03's closure members), M evaluations reused only after the checks; 5 fit/timing probes for all four arms at 32 × 2 with a defined projection, both-backbone M parity on loss/gradients/buffers/RNG and an allowlisted args/environment diff, GPU requirement stated; 6 exact integer counts, matching tolerance ≤ 0.5 %, trainable = requires_grad = full − 20; 7 cohort rules for curve points, targets and comparison cells with exclusion reporting and empty-cell refusal; 8 timing basis corrected (measured 0.91 s per micro-batch; 43 h is the 1.4 s bound), yaw blocks budgeted for all six arms at seed 42, cumulative attempt ceiling 1.5 × projection; 9 H1 verdict wording scoped per metric and to the tested tiers.

## 12. v3 changelog (responses to the round-2 plan review)

